# ------------------------- from the independent review of these fixes

[break] program-search-looks-in-relative-entries
rule: A program the harness starts by name (its shell, git) is looked for in the absolute directories of PATH only. The search checks twice, the directory and then the path a name makes with it (a name with a drive and no root replaces the directory), so the break takes both checks out.
file: crates/cortex-base/src/program.rs
in: find
find:
    .filter(|directory| directory.is_absolute())
    .flat_map(|directory| names.iter().map(move |name| directory.join(name)))
    .find(|candidate| candidate.is_absolute() && is_program(candidate, windows))
replace:
    .flat_map(|directory| names.iter().map(move |name| directory.join(name)))
    .find(|candidate| is_program(candidate, windows))
packages: cortex-base, cortex-tools
caught-by:
    cortex-base program::tests::a_relative_path_entry_does_not_make_a_file_there_the_program
    cortex-tools::it shell_search::sys_a_relative_path_entry_does_not_make_a_file_there_the_shell

[break] session-store-starts-git-by-name
rule: The session store starts git by the path found in an absolute directory of PATH, never by its bare name. Until the third tooling step a test could not give its process a PATH with a relative entry, and the break survived; the test kit's rerun helper gives a child one (Linux only: the planted git is a shell script).
file: crates/cortex-session/src/base.rs
in: SystemGit::run
find: let mut child = Command::new(program)
replace: let _ = program; let mut child = Command::new("git")
caught-by:
    cortex-session::it base::sys_git_is_never_found_through_a_relative_path_entry

[break] drive-relative-shell-looked-up-as-a-name
rule: On Windows a configured shell with a drive and no root (`C:bash.exe`) is a relative path, refused. Its test is Windows-only (`shell_search::on_windows_a_shell_named_with_a_drive_and_no_root_is_refused`, run in CI and windows-try), and on Linux such a name is one plain file name, so a run of the breaks at a Linux desk sees nothing.
file: crates/cortex-tools/src/shell/kind.rs
in: ShellSearch::find
find: program.contains(['/', '\\']) || !plain
replace: program.contains(['/', '\\']) || (!plain && false)
expect: survives

[break] non-user-sets-what-is-the-users-alone
rule: A non-user client's overrides may set only preferences and choices that raise cost: what is the user's alone (a provider's address, the shell, the data directory) is refused.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/core.rs
in: only_preferences
find: Trust::Preference | Trust::RaisesCost | Trust::BySpeed
replace: Trust::Preference | Trust::RaisesCost | Trust::BySpeed | Trust::UserOnly | Trust::RunsCode | Trust::WidensAccess
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it settings::a_supervisor_cannot_start_a_session_above_the_level_it_could_set

[break] user-configuration-file-left-open
rule: The user's configuration file is closed to reading and writing wherever `CORTEX_CONFIG` puts it. It is closed as named and where it leads, which for a file that is not a link are one path, so the break takes both out.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/assemble.rs
in: engine_parts
find:
    if let Some(file) = dirs.user_config.as_deref() {
        if let Some(named) = resolve_dir(file) {
            protected = protected.closed(named);
        }
        if let Some(target) = std::fs::canonicalize(file)
            .ok()
            .and_then(|target| AbsPath::from_os(&target).ok())
        {
            protected = protected.closed(target);
        }
    }
replace:
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it start::the_users_configuration_file_is_closed_wherever_it_is_kept

[break] linked-configuration-file-open-where-it-leads
rule: A configuration file that is a link is closed where it leads too.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/assemble.rs
in: engine_parts
find:
    if let Some(target) = std::fs::canonicalize(file)
        .ok()
        .and_then(|target| AbsPath::from_os(&target).ok())
    {
        protected = protected.closed(target);
    }
replace:
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it start::a_configuration_file_that_is_a_link_is_closed_where_it_leads
